&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Affirm is reinventing credit to make it more honest and friendly, giving consumers the flexibility to buy now and pay later without any hidden fees or compounding interest.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Affirm is building its own bank — and this role sits in the engineering team that runs it. We&#39;re looking for a Senior Software Engineer to join a deliberately small, AI-native team that owns the systems behind Affirm&#39;s bank: vendor-integrated banking infrastructure, durable workflows, data platform, and the operational tooling that holds it all together. You&#39;ll work alongside other senior engineers, with direct exposure to senior bank and Affirm leadership, to launch the bank&#39;s deposit product, drive loan originations through the bank entity, and bring card issuing online in time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a rare opportunity to shape a new business from its very first systems — a startup-like build inside an established company. You&#39;ll be one of the first engineers on Affirm&#39;s bank, moving with the speed, autonomy, and ownership of an early-stage team while leveraging Affirm&#39;s brand, distribution, and consumer reach. The team is small and AI-native, the surface area is broad, and the work meaningfully matters — every system you ship serves real customers under a real bank charter. The systems you build and the standards you set will directly determine what the bank becomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own bank systems end-to-end.&lt;/strong&gt; Design, build, integrate, operate, and own incident response for the bank&#39;s core technical surfaces: cloud infrastructure, data platform, durable workflow orchestration, core banking configuration, CI/CD, networking, and the Bank ↔ Affirm Inc integration. Generalist breadth is expected.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be a force multiplier on a small team.&lt;/strong&gt; Set and improve code review and design standards, lift the bar on examiner-readable documentation, and make the team you join more effective than the team you found. Every Senior IC on this team has outsized influence on what gets built and how.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ship AI-first.&lt;/strong&gt; Lean on AI tools and agentic workflows as a multiplier for code, design review, runbook generation, and operations. Push yourself and your teammates on what an AI-leveraged team can deliver.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own vendor relationships.&lt;/strong&gt; Carry one or more of the bank&#39;s third-party vendor relationships end-to-end — integration, operations, escalation, and audit. The bank&#39;s tech stack is intentionally vendor-leveraged, and ownership of those relationships is an engineering responsibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build for examiners.&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with Legal, Compliance, Risk, and Internal Audit to factor in compliance from day one. Write decisions, designs, and runbooks to a standard that holds up under examiner and audit review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the operational posture of your work.&lt;/strong&gt; Set up monitoring, alerting, runbooks, and the practices that keep the bank&#39;s systems reliable, observable, and audit-ready. The bank operates with a small operational footprint by design — help keep it that way.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Influence beyond the team.&lt;/strong&gt; Communicate technical strategy, tradeoffs, and constraints clearly to non-engineering stakeholders (bank executives, Compliance, Risk), and engineers outside the bank. The bank doesn&#39;t operate in isolation, and the relationships you build with non-bank engineers shape how cleanly the integration boundary works.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Help grow talent as the team grows.&lt;/strong&gt; As new engineers join over time, they&#39;ll join an engineering function whose practices and standards you helped establish. Provide feedback, mentor peers, and lead by example.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What We Look For&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of software engineering experience, with senior-strong, hands-on builder credentials and a track record of taking ownership end-to-end through launch and operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comfortable in ambiguity&lt;/strong&gt; — you move fast, ask hard questions, and take ownership before being asked, while balancing speed with engineering judgment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bias toward simplicity&lt;/strong&gt; — experience operating in or building toward a small, lean engineering culture where the engineering bar is high and the surface area is kept intentionally tight&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hungry to leverage AI to drive outcomes&lt;/strong&gt; — fluent with AI-assisted development tools (Claude, Cursor, Codex, agentic workflows) and actively pushing yourself and your team to use them as a multiplier for code quality, velocity, and what a deliberately small team can ship&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong systems thinking&lt;/strong&gt; across public cloud infrastructure (AWS preferred), infrastructure-as-code (Terraform), and cloud data platforms (Snowflake or comparable)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regulated-environment experience&lt;/strong&gt; — direct work in banking, payments, securities, healthcare, or another setting subject to external examination, where the work involves examiner-facing documentation and decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comfortable as the technical face of your work&lt;/strong&gt; to non-engineering stakeholders — Compliance, Risk, Finance, outside counsel, and examiners — and able to document decisions so they hold up under audit review&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exceptional written and verbal communication&lt;/strong&gt; — you can distill complex technical, regulatory, and operational concepts into clear narratives for executives and non-engineering audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This position requires either equivalent practical experience or a Bachelor’s degree in a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Nice to have&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior work inside a bank, neobank, Banking-as-a-Service provider, card issuer/processor, or fintech with a chartered bank subsidiary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience with a de novo bank launch, an early-stage bank buildout, or a greenfield regulated platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with a bank core, card processing / issuer processor integration, or digital bank experience integration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience standing up a greenfield cloud organization — fresh cloud org, IAM model, and data platform — under a tight security posture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with the regulatory framework that shapes the work: FDIC examinations, GLBA / Reg P (affiliate data sharing), BSA/AML, Reg E, Reg DD, Reg Z, model risk, and third-party risk management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
